01_07_00_54_55	Debug: {'system_prompt': '\n        You are a Fight The Landlord (Dou Dizhu) player. \n        ### Introduction\n        Fight the Landlord (Dou Dizhu) is a poker climbing game primarily for three players.\n        ### Players, Cards and Deal\n        This game uses a 54-card pack including two jokers, red and black. The cards rank from high to low:\n        red joker, black joker, 2, A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3. Suits are irrelevant.\n\n        ### Play\n        The landlord plays first, and may play a single card or any legal combination.\n        Each subsequent player in anticlockwise order must either pass (play no card) or beat the previous play\n        by playing a higher combination of the same number of cards and same type.\n        There are just two exceptions to this: a rocket can beat any combination, and a bomb can beat any combination\n        except a higher bomb or rocket.\n\n        ### Combinations\n        1. Single card: ranking from three (low) up to red joker (high).\n        2. Pair: two cards of the same rank, from three (low) up to two (high).\n        3. Triplet: three cards of the same rank.\n        4. Triplet with an attached card: a triplet with any single card added.\n        5. Triplet with an attached pair: a triplet with a pair added.\n        6. Sequence: at least five cards of consecutive rank, from 3 up to ace. Twos and jokers cannot be used.\n        7. Sequence of pairs: at least three pairs of consecutive ranks, from 3 up to ace. Twos and jokers cannot be used.\n        8. Sequence of triplets: at least two triplets of consecutive ranks from three up to ace.\n        9. Sequence of triplets with attached cards: an extra card is added to each triplet.\n        10. Sequence of triplets with attached pairs: an extra pair is attached to each triplet.\n        11. Bomb: four cards of the same rank. Beats everything except a rocket and a higher bomb.\n        12. Rocket: a pair of jokers. The highest combination, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Previous Player (Left) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Next Player (Right) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♠3 ♥3 ♦4 ♥5 ♦5 ♣6 ♣7 ♦7 ♣8 ♠9 ♥J ♠Q ♥Q ♥A ♠2 ♣2 BlackJoker\nLast Play to Beat: ♦2\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 1 (Prev Player): ♠4 ♥4 ♣4 ♠7 ♥7\nTurn 1 (You): Pass\nTurn 2 (Next Player): ♣3 ♦3 ♠6 ♥6 ♦6\nTurn 2 (Prev Player): ♠10 ♥10 ♦10 ♠A ♣A\nTurn 2 (You): Pass\nTurn 3 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 3 (Prev Player): ♠8 ♥8 ♦8 ♥9\nTurn 3 (You): Pass\nTurn 4 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 4 (Prev Player): ♦J ♠K ♥K ♦K\nTurn 4 (You): Pass\nTurn 5 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 5 (Prev Player): ♦2\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 12\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 1\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nRedJoker: 1, 2: 1, A: 1, K: 1, Q: 2, J: 2, 10: 1, 9: 2, 5: 2\nValid Moves:\nsingle: BlackJoker\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': "**Strategic Imperative: Neutralize the Landlord**\n\nAlright, the pressure's on. The Landlord just threw down a ♦2, and they're down to their last card. As a Peasant, my priority is to stop the Landlord from winning this round. The situation is dire; if I pass and my teammate can't beat the 2, we lose. However, if I can secure the win this trick, the Landlord's chances of winning this round goes to 0 (unless they have the Red Joker, but if so, it's already over, no matter what).\n\nConsidering my hand, the Black Joker is the only play that guarantees me this trick. It's a high card, and I can play it to ensure the Landlord cannot take control. The valid moves are telling me I can play the Black Joker as a single, and that is what I must do. If the Landlord has the Red Joker as their last card, we're toast no matter what, but that's a gamble I have to take. It's the only play that keeps us in the game, so there is no reason to pass.\n\nIf I play Black Joker, the Landlord must pass (or lose). Then it is my turn again.\nMy cards include pairs (33, 55, 77, QQ, and 22), so after I beat the Landlord with the Black Joker, I can play a pair or a straight (3-4-5-6-7-8-9) or one of my other cards to prevent the Landlord from doing anything. If I get the lead, the Landlord can't do anything because they only have 1 card. The Landlord can only watch me and my teammate play, which means victory!\n\nThe only logical move, therefore, is to play the Black Joker. It's the only way to stop the Landlord, and the JSON output confirms it. After this, all I need to do is lead a combo that the Landlord cannot beat and victory is certain.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord has played a high card (♦2) and has only 1 card remaining. This is a critical moment. If the Landlord wins this trick, they will play their final card and win the game. I hold the Black Joker, which beats the ♦2. I cannot rely on my teammate to beat the 2, as they might not have the Red Joker or a Bomb. By playing the Black Joker, I prevent the Landlord from winning immediately. Furthermore, since the Landlord only has a single card left, once I gain the lead, I can play combinations like Pairs or Straights that the Landlord cannot respond to, effectively locking them out of the game and allowing my teammate and me to clear our hands.\n\nReason: The Landlord is threatening to win with 1 card left. I must use the Black Joker to block the 2 and seize control of the game to prevent the Landlord from playing their final card.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["BlackJoker"]}'}
